config CENTAURI
	tristate "Apple Centauri Wi-Fi/Bluetooth Rust bring-up driver"
	depends on RUST && ARM64 && OF && PCI && PCI_MSI && BT && CFG80211
	help
	  Rust hardware and DMA queue driver for Apple Centauri PCI functions
	  described by enabled device-tree nodes. The cold path owns firmware
	  image transfer, port reset/removal/rescan, radio queues and interface
	  activation using normal Linux PCI/DMA APIs. Passive 2.4GHz scanning,
	  WPA2/CCMP association with an ordinary supplicant supplying the PMK,
	  SAE/default-PWE or H2E-only with required PMF, and native Ethernet
	  traffic work. H2E-only checks peer RSNXE and rejects observed legacy
	  commits; forced hunting/pecking is unsupported. passive_scan is required
	  for this experimental scan path.
	  Cold Bluetooth generates its own HCI command/event and ACL rings.
	  Firmware inputs are prepared independently outside the driver. Wider
	  protocol coverage, automatic chip-power sequencing and initial host PHY
	  integration remain incomplete.

	  Separate experimental warm Wi-Fi nodes can register Ethernet
	  transports from current-boot typed loader metadata. That older path
	  requires a stopped previous owner and reserved DMA pages, and does not
	  prove independent cold startup or association.
